This extension adds AC IV Black Flag modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Ubisoft Connect[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Installs AnvilToolkit itself, recognised by an "anviltoolkit.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Installs ResoRep itself, recognised by a "d3d11.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".dds" file to the "ResoRep\modded" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "version.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "dlc_1" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with an "Extracted" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "<name>.forge" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "<name>.data" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".data" file.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".forge" file.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "videos" folder to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above is installed to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

